Nothing else in your list was sufficiently useful to be more attractive
to me than immunity to Pestilence's touch-of-disease attack, given that
tattoos as described are both risky and costly.  Even the risk of
getting a death-tattoo (and thus maybe being deathrayed) instead of a
pestilence-tattoo isn't big enough; I'd just make sure I had an AoLS
before I went to the tattooist.

Essentially, either your rider tattoos are too powerful (because a
well-prepared character not playing conducts would always reach a point
where they could more-or-less safely get one at a modest cost in
resources) or they are too dangerous (because the risk is sufficiently
large to endanger even a well-prepared character), so either I'd (almost)
always take Pestilence (if I could cast cure sickness at 0% in my
ascension kit, or if I was a wizard with the Finger, I wouldn't bother)
or I'd never take any of them.

The +n tattoo is too risky, due to the chance of it frying my armour
when I get dressed after a (possibly forced) liaison with a foocubus
and the risk of getting a '-7' instead of a '+7'.

The luck-skew tattoos are a crapshoot with no great merit.  The divine
tattoos are just weird (and again, the penalty from a mistake by the
tattooist is too large).

The "getting it wrong" hazard from a scroll tattoo might just kill you.

